          "text": "{\"matches\":[{\"id\":\"ledger-sales-total\",\"title\":\"CSV ledger aggregation pattern (read export.json params first)\",\"content\":\"Task pattern: \\\"total amount of sales rows in ledger.csv export\\\".\\nSteps: ALWAYS read export.json first — it holds parser params (encoding, delimiter, preamble_lines, file). Do not assume UTF-8/comma/no-preamble: seen cases with {\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf-16\\\",\\\"delimiter\\\":\\\"\\\\t\\\",\\\"preamble_lines\\\":2}.\\nCall parse_csv(path, encoding=export.encoding, delimiter=export.delimiter, skip_lines=export.preamble_lines). Note: a raw tab in JSON makes the parser emit \\\"\\\\t\\\" which fails with TypeError \\\"delimiter must be a 1-character string\\\" — pass delimiter as the two-character escape \\\"\\\\t\\\" (backslash-t) so it decodes to a real tab.\\nledger.csv columns = category,amount; rows alternate sales/refund. \\\"total amount of sales rows\\\" = SUM(amount) over rows where category==\\\"sales\\\" (a sum, not a row count). Example: sales 12,30,48,66 -> 156. Amounts may be strings in the raw rows; cast/round to number.\\nAlways emit result as {\\\"answer\\\": number}.\",\"version\":3}],\"index\":\"synchronous current-version lexical search\",\"total_entries\":2}"
